quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  3,30,"The Day (will surely come) when every soul shall find present (before it) whatever good it has done. And whatever evil it has perpetrated, it will wish there was a great distance between it and that evil. Allah warns you to beware of (disobeying) Him, and Allah is Most-Kind towards (His) servants."
  3,31,"(O Esteemed Prophet!) Say: ‘If you love Allah, then follow me; Allah will love you and forgive you your sins, and Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful.’"
  3,32,"Say: ‘Obey Allah and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him).’ But if they turn away, then Allah does not like the disbelievers."
  3,33,"Indeed, Allah chose Adam and Nuh (Noah) and the descendants of Ibrahim (Abraham) and the descendants of ‘Imran above all the nations,"
  3,34,"as offspring, one from another. And Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
  3,35,"And (recall) when the wife of ‘Imran (Maryam’s father) said: ‘My Lord, I dedicate to You what is in my womb, freeing him (of worldly obligations). So accept it from me. Indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.’"
  3,36,"And when she delivered a baby girl, she said: ‘My Lord, I have given birth to a female.’ But Allah knew very well what she had given birth to; the male (she prayed for) was not like the female (that Allah had blessed her with). (She further said:) ‘I have named her Maryam (Mary—the worshipper). And indeed, I commend her and her offspring to Your care against (the evil of) the accursed Satan.’"
  3,37,"So her Lord accepted her with gracious favour, made her grow in a worthy upbringing and entrusted her to the care of Zakariyya (Zachariah). Whenever Zakariyya (Zachariah) visited her in the prayer chamber, he would find provisions with her (i.e. novel food items and out-of-season fruit). He said: ‘O Maryam, from where has this come to you?’ She said: ‘It comes from Allah. Indeed Allah provides for whomever He pleases without measure.’"
